Hard routing cases for lane diagrams (WO-62). Each case starts with a "<!-- case: name -->"
line and is a map of its own; test/lanes.js lays each out and checks its arrows.

<!-- case: three-way-decision -->
# Three-way decision

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  ask[Ask] --> q{Which team?}
  q -->|sales| s[Quote]
  q -->|support| t[Fix]
  q -->|billing| b[Refund]
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- desk : Desk
- sales : Sales
- support : Support
- billing : Billing

### Placement
- ask, q : desk
- s : sales
- t : support
- b : billing

<!-- case: chained-decisions -->
# Chained decisions

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  a[Order] --> q1{In stock?}
  q1 -->|yes| q2{Paid?}
  q1 -->|no| back[Back order]
  q2 -->|yes| ship[Ship]
  q2 -->|no| chase[Chase payment]
  chase --> q2
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- shop : Shop
- money : Finance
- store : Warehouse

### Placement
- a, q1 : shop
- q2, chase : money
- back, ship : store

<!-- case: up-and-down-in-one-gap -->
# Up and down in one gap

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  a[Top start] --> d[Bottom end]
  b[Bottom start] --> c[Top end]
  e[Middle start] --> f[Middle end]
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- one : One
- two : Two
- three : Three
- four : Four

### Placement
- a, c : one
- e, f : two
- b, d : four

<!-- case: many-in-one-gap -->
# Many arrows in one gap

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  hub[Dispatch] --> l1[One]
  hub --> l2[Two]
  hub --> l3[Three]
  hub --> l4[Four]
  hub --> l5[Five]
  hub --> l6[Six]
  hub --> l7[Seven]
  hub --> l8[Eight]
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- r1 : R1
- r2 : R2
- r3 : R3
- r4 : R4
- r5 : R5
- r6 : R6
- r7 : R7
- r8 : R8

### Placement
- hub, l1 : r1
- l2 : r2
- l3 : r3
- l4 : r4
- l5 : r5
- l6 : r6
- l7 : r7
- l8 : r8

<!-- case: back-arrows -->
# Back arrows

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  a[Draft] --> b[Review]
  b --> q{Approved?}
  q -->|no| a
  q -->|yes| c[Publish]
  c --> d[Audit]
  d -->|issue| b
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- author : Author
- editor : Editor
- legal : Legal

### Placement
- a : author
- b, q, c : editor
- d : legal

<!-- case: crowded-cell -->
# Crowded cell

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  in1[In one] --> x1[Check A]
  in2[In two] --> x2[Check B]
  x1 --> x2
  x2 --> x3[Check C]
  x3 --> out[Done]
  x1 --> out
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- top : Top
- mid : Middle
- low : Low

### Columns
- before : Before
- during : During
- after : After

### Placement
- in1 : top : before
- in2 : low : before
- x1, x2, x3 : mid : during
- out : top : after

<!-- case: shared-entry -->
# Shared entry

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  a[Start] --> q{Ok?}
  q -->|yes| p[Proceed]
  q -->|no| r[Rework]
  x[Other] --> y[Prepare]
  y --> r
```

## Lanes

### Rows
- main : Main
- side : Side

### Placement
- a, q, p : main
- x, y, r : side

